{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1005116-lair-traits-and-extreme-environments","id":1005116,"title":"Lair Traits and Extreme Environments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-18T14:50:52-08:00","id":1005116,"title":"Lair Traits and Extreme Environments","content":"Many Lair traits say they count as Extreme Environments (Hurricane, Extreme Cold, Extreme Heat, etc), but also include rules that don't really align with the Extreme Environment rules.<br /> <br /> For example: Hurricane counts as a level 3 extreme environment. In addition to the damage, this levels a -3 penalty to all actions. However, the text than says it 'also' imposes a -3 to aural Perception rolls and all Physical Dice Pools.<br /> <br /> Which of the following interpretations are correct?<br /> <br /> 1) -3 to all actions in the effected area, increased to -6 for aural perception rolls and physical dice pools. This is an extremely high penalty, but...it is a Hurricane.<br /> 2) -3 to aural perception rolls and physical dice pools only, replacing the usual -3 to all actions. Seems underpowered, but my instinct is this may be RAI","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:12:49-08:00","id":1005988,"title":"","content":"Hmm . . . I don't have my copy handy, but you might be able to reconcile the discrepancy do to the origin of a Chamber. Its not a &quot;real&quot; place - rather, its a tangible representation of a human's reaction to a real world event. So a hurricane-themed Chamber might well have different rules than a &quot;real&quot; hurricane would","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:37:06-08:00","id":1006002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1005116-lair-traits-and-extreme-environments?p=1005988#post1005988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm . . . I don't have my copy handy, but you might be able to reconcile the discrepancy do to the origin of a Chamber. Its not a &quot;real&quot; place - rather, its a tangible representation of a human's reaction to a real world event. So a hurricane-themed Chamber might well have different rules than a &quot;real&quot; hurricane would</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the rules describing the Hurricane Lair trait say that it both counts as a Level 3 Extreme Environment, and imposes the -3 penalty. There's no actual discrepancy, as the Lair Trait does mention both - I'm just not sure if they stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:02:54-08:00","id":1006156,"title":"","content":"With a straight reading of the relevant sections... I think they stack, so you have a -3 dice penalty to all actions and a -6 dice penalty to aural perception and physical rolls. <br /> <br /> That's pretty nasty, but Major Traits are noted as counting up to Level 4 Extreme Environments, and that's on par with desert exposure and moderate radiation exposure. Basically, stuff that will definitely kill you. <br /> <br /> Maybe they lowered the level of Extreme Environment for the more focused aspects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}